WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
So I want to take up on May 25th, 1915, and this is volume 11.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Men are obedient to governments which use violence, but they're not obedient to God, who uses love.

3
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Louisa said I was in my usual state when my beloved Jesus made himself seen for just a little.

4
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.000
And he said, my daughter, the scourge is great, we're in the middle of World War I, okay?

5
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Yet the people do not stir themselves, rather they remain almost indifferent,

6
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.000
as if they had to be present at a tragic scene, not a reality.

7
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Now this is something which is very, very, very important.

8
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:58.000
There's an extraordinary thing about human beings that you can see a tragedy on television,

9
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
or hear about a tragedy, and you say it's awful, but you're not really moved by it.

10
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.000
You don't really move to do anything.

11
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Because in the age that we're living in, we've got tragedy fatigue, there's just so much of it.

12
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.000
But there's a thing in the book of Revelation.

13
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.000
I think it's in chapter nine.

14
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.000
I looked it up and forgot to write it down.

15
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:31.000
I think it's in chapter nine, where it says that in the tribulation that the Lord sends,

16
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:36.000
the people who didn't experience it were done with their fornication, and their murdering,

17
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.000
and their this, and their that, and their the other.

18
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.000
In other words, if it didn't touch their own flesh, they continued sinning.

19
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.000
In other words, they learned nothing from it.

20
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.000
And this is the problem why the Lord permitted a world war.

21
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Everybody had to experience the punishment.

22
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.000
They weren't going to learn from watching somebody else.

23
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Isn't that amazing?

24
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.000
So watch it again now.

25
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.000
My daughter, the scourge is great.

26
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.000
That's World War I.

27
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Yet the people do not stir themselves.

28
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.000
In other words, there's no repentance.

29
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Rather, they remain almost indifferent, as if they had to be present at a tragic scene.

30
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Do you see what I mean?

31
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Not a reality.

32
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Instead of coming all unanimous to cry at my feet and implore mercy and forgiveness,

33
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.000
they stand at attention to hear what is happening.

34
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.000
In other words, we keep the news items going.

35
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.000
What's next?

36
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.000
What's happening now?

37
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.000
That's typical of us as humans.

38
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.000
And my daughter, how great is human perforty?

39
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Look at how obedient they are to governments.

40
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.000
Priests, lay people, do not demand anything.

41
00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.000
They do not refuse sacrifices.

42
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.000
And they must be ready to even give up their own life.

43
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:51.000
But for me, only there's no obedience and there's no sacrifices.

44
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.000
And if they did anything at all, it's more pretension and interests.

45
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.000
This, because the government uses violence and I use love.

46
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:03.000
In other words, the government forces you to do it.

47
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.000
Yet this love is disregarded by the people.

48
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.000
You remain indifferent as if I did not deserve anything from them.

49
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.000
So you can see that what's wrong with the people is their loss of faith

50
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.000
and their inability to discern the presence of God.

51
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.000
And as he was saying this, he burst into tears.

52
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.000
What a cruel torment Louisa said to see Jesus crying.

53
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.000
And then he continued, "But blood and fire will purify everything

54
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.000
and will restore the repentant man."

55
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.000
Now, in the Bible, fire is an image of chastisement.

56
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.000
It's an image of hell.

57
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.000
It's also an image of divine love, which is amazing.

58
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:50.000
In the first world where I looked this up,

59
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:56.000
there were approximately 19 million dead, according to the part of Google I looked up.

60
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.000
And it said 40 million casualties.

61
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.000
In other words, they don't say whether they were usually a casualty means dead, doesn't it?

62
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.000
So with all of this, people were not learning, isn't it amazing?

63
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Because as soon as World War I was over, they started behaving like they needed

64
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.000
another World War, which they did get.

65
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.000
So while saying this, Jesus showed Louisa the human carnage

66
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.000
for torment to live in these times, she said,

67
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.000
"What made the divine volition be always done?"

68
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.000
So when the Lord shows her everything, that's Amos 3.7,

69
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.000
the Lord shows the prophets everything ahead of time.

70
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.000
So June the 6th, 1915,

71
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:46.000
"In the divine will, everything resolves into love of God and one's neighbor."

72
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.000
Now, this is a VIP message,

73
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:55.000
because I keep telling you that the summary of the 36 volumes is divine will and love.

74
00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:00.000
And if divine will people are not actively loving,

75
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.000
then they are contradicting their claim that they're in the divine will.

76
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:10.000
That's why the law I have laid down in all our gatherings is that if you don't love, go home.

77
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:16.000
Because it would be a contradiction in terms, that love serves.

78
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:22.000
So Jesus said, "Everything resolves into love because God is love."

79
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:27.000
That's 1 John 4.7.

80
00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:34.000
And Louisa said, "As I am in my usual state, my beloved Jesus,

81
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:40.000
while remaining hidden, wants me all intent on him to plead continuously for my brothers."

82
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.000
That's for the rest of the human race.

83
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:47.000
And she's thinking particularly of everyone involved in the war.

84
00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:52.000
So while I was praying and crying for the salvation of the poor combatants,

85
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.000
is he what I mean? She's really praying for those in war.

86
00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Wanting to cling to Jesus so as to implore him that none of them would be lost,

87
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.000
I reached the point of speaking nonsense to him.

88
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.000
And Jesus, though sad, seemed to be pleased with my petitions.

89
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.000
And as though willing to concede what I wanted,

90
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:16.000
that means to save the lives of the soldiers who had given their lives for their country.

91
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.000
And he would accept that as a gift to him.

92
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.000
But a thought flew into my mind that I should think about my own salvation.

93
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.000
There's a mistake. For her, this is a very serious temptation.

94
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.000
Okay. Because we're not allowed to think of ourselves.

95
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:38.000
So Jesus said, "My daughter, as you were thinking about yourself,

96
00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:45.000
you produced a human sensation and my will is fully divine

97
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:54.000
and noticed it. In my will, everything resolves into love from me and your neighbor."

98
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.000
There's the two parts of the law. If you look at my hands,

99
00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.000
to love God and love your neighbor, and it makes the big "L" shape.

100
00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:06.000
Now, in Genesis 3, when they broke their relationship with God,

101
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.000
Genesis 4 shows you the first murder.

102
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:15.000
We're not actually able to love one another unless we're in love with God.

103
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:19.000
And the more in love with God we are, the more we can love one another.

104
00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:24.000
It's about that simple because it's God's love coming through us that goes out to our neighbor.

105
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.000
That's what it is. And so that's why I give you that "L" shape.

106
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.000
I think it's actually terribly important.

107
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:36.000
In my will, everything resolves into love for me and love for one's neighbor.

108
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:41.000
There are no personal things. We have got that clear, haven't we?

109
00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:49.000
Because by containing my will alone, the soul contains all possible goods for herself.

110
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.000
And if she contains them, why would you ask for them?

111
00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:56.000
You see, so if we're still asking for something personal for ourselves,

112
00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.000
we're not grasping what the divine will actually is.

113
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:05.000
Because if you have the fullness, why would you want a tiny bit?

114
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:11.000
If you win the lottery, it wouldn't be going down to the ATM for 10 euros, would you?

115
00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.000
No. You have the whole lot.

116
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.000
So that's what he's saying. You have everything.

117
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.000
So why would you go looking for little bitsies?

118
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:26.000
Because by containing my will alone, the soul contains all possible goods for herself.

119
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:30.000
And if she contains them, why ask me for them?

120
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.000
Rather, isn't it right that she occupy herself with praying for those who don't have them?

121
00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:38.000
Now, do you see the issue?

122
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:43.000
If you knew what calamities, miserable humanity will go through,

123
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.000
you'd be more active in my will for their good.

124
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:54.000
And while saying this, Luisa said he made me hear all the evils that the masons were plotting against humanity.

125
00:08:54.000 --> 00:09:01.000
Now, you know, if you read our ladies' messages to Don Goby in the blue book, to my beloved priests.

126
00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:07.000
She said that ecclesiastical masonry was what was destroying the church.

127
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.000
I'm saying that because of this.

128
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:20.000
And so it was the masons infiltrated by the Illuminati that were bringing all the damage to the world, and still are.

129
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.000
Okay. But I'm amazed that she actually named it.

130
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.000
Normally she just says sects.

131
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.000
She doesn't actually name them. But here she names them.

132
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:36.000
So, June the 17th, 1915, everything must end in divine will.

133
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:39.000
Now, we've just heard everything must end in divine love.

134
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.000
Now, divine will and divine love are together.

135
00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.000
Okay.

136
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:48.000
Finding myself in my usual state, I was lamenting to Jesus, saying to him,

137
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:51.000
"My life, Jesus, everything is ended.

138
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:56.000
There's nothing left from me, but your flashes and shadows at the most."

139
00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:02.000
And Jesus interrupting me, my book says interrupting my speaking, which is not English.

140
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:09.000
Interrupting me said, "My daughter, everything must end in my will."

141
00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:13.000
Because everything began in the divine will, so everything has to end there.

142
00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.000
Once the soul has reached this, she's done everything.

143
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:19.000
That really needs to be colored if you have a color.

144
00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:22.000
You've done everything once you're doing the divine will.

145
00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:30.000
And if she had done much and had not enclosed it in my will,

146
00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.000
one can say she's done nothing.

147
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:36.000
Is that okay?

148
00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:40.000
In other words, all the value is in the divine will.

149
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:46.000
In fact, I take into account all that ends in my will.

150
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.000
Now, I love the way he says all that ends in my will,

151
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:55.000
because you might discover at a particular moment that you forgot to put your axe in the divine will.

152
00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:59.000
I say, "Oh Lord, for the little bits I've forgotten, I've put them in as well."

153
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.000
You're not supposed to end in the divine will.

154
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:08.000
Because the divine will alone is my very life present.

155
00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:12.000
That is the divine life is present in the divine will.

156
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:17.000
And if you're living in the divine will, the divine will is present in you.

157
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:20.000
Okay?

158
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:25.000
My very life is present as though bound.

159
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:29.000
And so it is right that I take into account even the littlest things

160
00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:35.000
and even trifles as my own things, because in each little act that the creature does united with my will,

161
00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:41.000
I feel that she first takes it from me and then she operates.

162
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:46.000
So it doesn't matter how small the action is, even if I just pick up this pen off the table.

163
00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:52.000
It doesn't matter how tiny it is, if it's in the divine will, it's huge.

164
00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:57.000
So this is a very important piece about the value of divine acts.

165
00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:08.000
So her little act comprises the whole of my sanctity, power, wisdom, and love all that I am.

166
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:16.000
And in that act done united with my will, I feel my life, my works, my word, my thought, and so on

167
00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:21.000
being repeated in every little act that's done in the divine will.

168
00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:27.000
So that's why you have to put a VIP on that paragraph apart from the entire message.

169
00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:34.000
So if your things have ended in my will, what else would you want?

170
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:38.000
All things have only one final point.

171
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:43.000
When everybody dies, they are locked into the divine will permanently.

172
00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.000
That's it.

173
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:52.000
And so the problem is that if they went into that position in a wrong place with God,

174
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.000
they only meet the judgment end of the divine will.

175
00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:05.000
If you die in the position of surrender to the divine will, you're going into the beatitude end of the divine will

176
00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:09.000
because we live between the judgment of God and the mercy of God.

177
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:15.000
Just like a child lives between the cuddles of the parent and the discipline of the parent.

178
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.000
Isn't that correct?

179
00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.000
They're the two stop points.

180
00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:30.000
Everybody in society lives between society offering you honors because of the wonderful stuff that you're doing

181
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.000
and a prison cell for those who are absolutely rebellious.

182
00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.000
And again, it's the same thing.

183
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.000
It's the mercy or the justice.

184
00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:49.000
And where it comes to an extremely serious point is if you die at the wrong end of that scale,

185
00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:53.000
whatever end of it you're at, you have it forever.

186
00:13:53.000 --> 00:14:00.000
We can't explain enough how important it is to die well.

187
00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:06.000
So all things have only one final point.

188
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:13.000
The sun has only one point that its light may invade all the earth.

189
00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:19.000
The farmer's soul's hose works the earth and suffers from cold and heat, but this is not the final point.

190
00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:25.000
No, his point is to reap the fruits and to make them into food.

191
00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:31.000
The same for many other things which many as they are, they all resolve into a single point.

192
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.000
And this constitutes the life of man.

193
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:41.000
In the same way, the soul must make everything end in the single point of my will.

194
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:45.000
Notice the single point, there's neither past nor future.

195
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.000
Okay.

196
00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:50.000
And my will will constitute her life.

197
00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:57.000
So you will be in the divine moment in every act that you do in the divine will.

198
00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.000
You're in the divine moment.

199
00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:04.000
And I will make of it my food, he said.

200
00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:15.000
So in the next short paragraph, Louisa begins to recognize that she's being lifted up onto a higher plane.

201
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:18.000
She had human sufferings, physical sufferings before.

202
00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:23.000
The Lord is going to bring her into spiritual sufferings, divine sufferings.

203
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:31.000
Then Jesus added, "In these sad times you and I will go through a very painful period because things will rage more."

204
00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:36.000
You see, the problem about a war is that it releases the demons.

205
00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:40.000
And so you have much more than what human beings are doing.

206
00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.000
You have the demons on top of that.

207
00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:47.000
So human anger is then multiplied and terrible things happen.

208
00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:53.000
Resentment and bitterness and all the negative stuff is all multiplied because the demons are present.

209
00:15:53.000 --> 00:16:02.000
And therefore, in a war, unspeakable things happen, things that you'd say no human being could do that.

210
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:09.000
Like for example, they experimented on living human beings in the concentration camps.

211
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:16.000
And some of the medical knowledge we have today is at the cost of those people.

212
00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:22.000
That regardless of whether they were going to live or die, this experiment was done on them.

213
00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:27.000
So some of the medicine we have today is at the cost of a person's life.

214
00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.000
I don't think it's worth it.

215
00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.000
Anyway, so things will rage more.

216
00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:41.000
But know that if I take my cross of wood away from you, I give you the cross of my will.

217
00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:47.000
The cross of wood is the sufferings as you have experienced them in the past, human sufferings.

218
00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:51.000
I'll give you the cross of my will, which is totally spiritual.

219
00:16:51.000 --> 00:17:01.000
Now, the cross of the divine will is given to us all because things happen to us that are not what we want

220
00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:08.000
and surrendering completely to the divine will is the big sacrifice that you make.

221
00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:13.000
I give you the cross of my will, which has no length and no width.

222
00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:16.000
It is interminable.

223
00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:21.000
Okay, a more noble cross I could not give you. It is not made of wood.

224
00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:24.000
It's made of light.

225
00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:31.000
Because everything to do with God is light, one John, one five.

226
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:37.000
And it's one Timothy 616.

227
00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:41.000
God lives in unapproachable light.

228
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:48.000
And in this light, burning more than fire, we will suffer together for each soul.

229
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.000
Now, I want you to notice that.

230
00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:53.000
There were millions of people out on those battlefields.

231
00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:59.000
I'm quite sure that most of those soldiers thought nobody was carrying one Iota about them.

232
00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:05.000
And there was Jesus and Louisa carrying for each one of them individually.

233
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:11.000
Now, if you go to the hours of the Passion and you come to the scourging of Jesus,

234
00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:19.000
you hear very clearly that Jesus made reparation for each individual sin one by one.

235
00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:23.000
That's why he was literally skinned like a lamb.

236
00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:28.000
I mean, the pain must have been beyond imagining, you know.

237
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:33.000
But here he says to Louisa we, that's Louisa and himself,

238
00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:37.000
we will suffer together for each one of them.

239
00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:45.000
And in their agonies and tortures, can you imagine there's this poor soldier dying out on a battlefield?

240
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.000
There's nobody around him. He thinks he's completely abandoned.

241
00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:53.000
And there's this wee soul down in Italy who doesn't know that man's name

242
00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:58.000
and is there spiritually to take him by the hand into eternity.

243
00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:04.000
Look at the divine mercy and divine love that's being manifested to us.

244
00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:08.000
That every single one is the same to him as the whole.

245
00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.000
It's utterly amazing.

246
00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:15.000
And that's why he tries to get us to do the hours of the Passion.

247
00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:18.000
I think we need to do the hours of the Passion very slowly.

248
00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:21.000
I can only take them sometimes a paragraph at a time.

249
00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:25.000
Because if you try and get into it and realize what he's doing,

250
00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:30.000
it enables you to rise to the occasion and say yes, yes, yes,

251
00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.000
I want to be in there totally with this.

252
00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.000
I just think this is fantastic.

253
00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:41.000
In this light burning more than fire because it's the fire of God's love.

254
00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:48.000
We will suffer together for each soul and in their agonies in tortures

255
00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:51.000
and we will try to be the life of them all.

256
00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:56.000
I think it's wonderful. It gives you a different picture to World War I and II, doesn't it?

257
00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.000
Okay.

258
00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:03.000
So July the 9th, 1915.

259
00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:07.000
One who truly does the divine will or lives in the divine will

260
00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:11.000
is placed in the same condition as the humanity of Christ.

261
00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:14.000
Even the heading is amazing.

262
00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.000
Okay.

263
00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:19.000
So, Louisa said, finding myself in my usual state,

264
00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:22.000
I was feeling very bad. You need to put bad in inverted commas.

265
00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:25.000
Bad has to do with how she feels.

266
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:30.000
It's nothing to do with sin because you can't be in the divine will and sin.

267
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:36.000
I was feeling very bad and my beloved Jesus moved to compassion for my poor state,

268
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:41.000
came for a little while kissing me and said, poor daughter, do not fear.

269
00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:45.000
I do not leave you nor can I leave you.

270
00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:50.000
That's because the union of their wills is one.

271
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:54.000
So you can't leave her. They have one will together.

272
00:20:54.000 --> 00:21:00.000
In fact, one who does my will is my magnet,

273
00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:05.000
which acts powerfully over me and draws me to itself with such violence

274
00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:07.000
that I cannot resist.

275
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:11.000
So how could God resist a little creature on the earth,

276
00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:15.000
being, in Louisa's case, the only one initially,

277
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:19.000
whose will was locked into the divine will,

278
00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:25.000
and therefore God would feel just as happy in that little soul as he does in heaven.

279
00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:30.000
Because what makes the blessed Trinity infinitely happy is that one will,

280
00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.000
binding them together.

281
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:38.000
It takes too much, he said, to rid myself of one who does my will,

282
00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:42.000
I would be ridding myself of myself if that was possible.

283
00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:47.000
So then he added, my daughter,

284
00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:49.000
one who truly does my will.

285
00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:54.000
Now notice he's using the word truly a little bit often, isn't he?

286
00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:57.000
So he kind of knows us, doesn't he?

287
00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:03.000
One who truly does my will is placed in the same condition as my humanity.

288
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:08.000
In other words, you become another Christ.

289
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:13.000
I was man and God.

290
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:19.000
As God, I contained within myself all the happiness, beatitudes and beauty

291
00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:24.000
and all the goods that I possess.

292
00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:28.000
On the one hand, my humanity participated in my divinity,

293
00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:33.000
and therefore it was blissful and happy and its beatific vision never escaped me.

294
00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:38.000
On the other hand, it's very Jewish, on the one hand and on the other hand.

295
00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:43.000
On the other hand, having taken upon myself the satisfaction of souls before divine justice,

296
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:49.000
my humanity was tormented by the clear sight of all sins.

297
00:22:49.000 --> 00:23:01.000
Okay, so first of all, I want to give you two Corinthians 5, 17.

298
00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:10.000
And then he becomes man, that's Philippians 2 verses 1 to 11.

299
00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:18.000
And he's really talking about the all-seeing eye of God.

300
00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:24.000
God sees everything and he knows everything and he's saying to us that as God,

301
00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:27.000
he had the clear vision of God, the beatific vision.

302
00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:33.000
As man, he had a very clear vision of sin because he's seeing it in God.

303
00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:40.000
Is that okay? And seeing sin in God, you see it as it is, not as we see it.

304
00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:46.000
And therefore, this vision of the holiness of God on the one hand

305
00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:50.000
and the vision of the sinfulness of the human race on the other

306
00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:54.000
caused him terrible interior agony.

307
00:23:54.000 --> 00:24:00.000
So you're getting an insight into the interior passion of the Lord.

308
00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:04.000
So he says, "My humanity was tormented by the clear sight of all sins."

309
00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:08.000
Notice clear sight, it was not fuzzy.

310
00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:13.000
And having to take them upon itself, that's the sacred humanity,

311
00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:19.000
to satisfy for them, Jesus' humanity felt the horror of each sin.

312
00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:21.000
Notice each one.

313
00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:25.000
We've just been saying that himself and Louisa were interceding for

314
00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:31.000
and suffering for each soldier out on World War I and the battlefields.

315
00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:40.000
We're being told that Jesus atoned for each sin with its own special torment.

316
00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:45.000
In other words, Jesus did our hell for us.

317
00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:49.000
Therefore, there's absolutely no reason why we should have to go there.

318
00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:51.000
He has paid the price.

319
00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:58.000
And a long time ago I was praying the passion with Jesus.

320
00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:06.000
And I said to him, "Since you paid for every single sin,

321
00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:11.000
what will you say to a soul who comes to you in judgment

322
00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:14.000
and they've not accepted anything

323
00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:16.000
and they've not allowed you to redeem them?"

324
00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:20.000
And you know they're going in the opposite direction to where they should be going.

325
00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:22.000
He said, "I will stand in front of them,

326
00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:24.000
crowned with thorns,

327
00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:27.000
scourged, carrying my cross,

328
00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:32.000
and I will say, was it not enough for you, my friend?"

329
00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:41.000
We have a very human image of judgment.

330
00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:44.000
Sort of somebody saying, "Out of my sight."

331
00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:45.000
You know what I mean?

332
00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:49.000
He said, "No, I stand in front of them as the crucified Savior

333
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:51.000
and say, wasn't it enough?

334
00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:54.000
Was there something else you needed?"

335
00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:59.000
And so the person going to hell would be in a terrible state,

336
00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:04.000
realizing that so much love had been given to them

337
00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:06.000
and who was completely unaccepted.

338
00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:12.000
So this is this kind of thing that you're looking at here.

339
00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:17.000
Therefore Jesus said, "I felt joy and pain at the same time,

340
00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:21.000
the joy of the beatific vision and the pain of that sin.

341
00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:23.000
Love on the part of my divinity,

342
00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:26.000
freezing cold on the part of souls.

343
00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:30.000
Sanctity on the one hand, sin on the other.

344
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:35.000
There was nothing which the soul would do that could escape me,

345
00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:40.000
that Sam 1 3 9 verses 1 to 5.

346
00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:44.000
Sam 1 3 9 verses 1 to 5.

347
00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:46.000
Nothing could escape me,

348
00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:51.000
be it even the littlest thing.

349
00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:55.000
There's the all-seeing eye of God.

350
00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:59.000
Now, my humanity is no longer capable of suffering

351
00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:02.000
because he's now in glory.

352
00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:07.000
That's Matthew 28 6, he is risen.

353
00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:14.000
And now my humanity is no longer capable of suffering.

354
00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:18.000
Therefore, I live in one who does my will.

355
00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:21.000
So each one of us becomes a little incarnation.

356
00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:22.000
Okay?

357
00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:26.000
The way some of the speakers in the Divine will put it is

358
00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:30.000
that he by locates himself into us.

359
00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.000
This is why on the one hand,

360
00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:36.000
the soul feels love, peace, firmness and good fortitude

361
00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:38.000
and the like, and on the other,

362
00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:40.000
coldness and bothers and tiredness.

363
00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:44.000
Well, I've taken out a PhD and that one.

364
00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:50.000
If the soul remains completely in my will and takes these things,

365
00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:55.000
okay, not as her own things,

366
00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:57.000
and as things that I myself suffer,

367
00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:59.000
she will not lose heart,

368
00:27:59.000 --> 00:28:01.000
she will compassionate me,

369
00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:04.000
and she will have the honor of sharing in my pains

370
00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:11.000
because she is nothing other than a veil that covers me.

371
00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:13.000
Now, the veil that covers me,

372
00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.000
there again you have the living host.

373
00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:16.000
Is that okay?

374
00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:19.000
The living host.

375
00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:23.000
And she will feel nothing but the butters

376
00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:27.000
and the pricks of the cold, but it is into me, into my heart,

377
00:28:27.000 --> 00:28:28.000
that they are driven.

378
00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:31.000
So I want to give you a few verses here.

379
00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:35.000
Matthew 5, 11.

380
00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:41.000
Matthew 10, 25.

381
00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:48.000
Philippians 1, 29.

382
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:53.000
And Colossians 1, 24.

383
00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:58.000
You'll notice that if you look up all the references I give you,

384
00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:01.000
that you'll be doing Bible study as well.

385
00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:05.000
And you'll find the two dovetailing in a most amazing way.

386
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:06.000
Okay.

387
00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:08.000
So July the 25th, 1915.

388
00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:11.000
How Jesus is unfortunate in love.

389
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:13.000
You know the way we sometimes say,

390
00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:15.000
"God, that guy is unfortunate in love."

391
00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:18.000
He never seems to get the right person.

392
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Continuing my usual state,

393
00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:23.000
I was lamenting to Jesus because of his usual privations.

394
00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:27.000
And he always kind, my book says benign,

395
00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:29.000
which is the word we don't use,

396
00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:32.000
always kind, compassionate me, telling me,

397
00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:35.000
"My daughter, be stalwart.

398
00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:37.000
Be strong, be bold.

399
00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:43.000
Be faithful to me in these times of tragedy."

400
00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:46.000
And these times of horrendous carnage

401
00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:49.000
and of intense bitterness in my heart.

402
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:51.000
And almost sobbing, he added,

403
00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:55.000
"My daughter, in these times that's World War I,

404
00:29:55.000 --> 00:29:59.000
I feel like a poor unfortunate.

405
00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:03.000
I feel unfortunate together with the one who is wounded in the battlefield."

406
00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:06.000
And there's the identification with Jesus.

407
00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:08.000
As far as he's concerned,

408
00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:10.000
he's dying on the battlefield.

409
00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:14.000
That's Acts 9, 4 to 5.

410
00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:19.000
If you persecute them, you persecute me, remember?

411
00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:25.000
Matthew 10, 40 to 42.

412
00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:28.000
And there's another one in Matthew 25,

413
00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:31.000
"Whatever you do to the least of my brethren you do to me."

414
00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:32.000
Do you remember that one?

415
00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:35.000
That's in Matthew 25.

416
00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:39.000
So he identifies with each one of us.

417
00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:44.000
He said, "I feel unfortunate together with the one who is wounded on the battlefield.

418
00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:50.000
Unfortunate for the one who dies in his own blood abandoned by awe."

419
00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:53.000
But of course he has somebody standing by his side,

420
00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:56.000
making sure somebody else is interceding for them.

421
00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:59.000
And don't you realize in these awful times that we're living in,

422
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:03.000
he's getting more and more and more people into the divine will,

423
00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:09.000
interceding for everybody and to intercede for them before the chastisement

424
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:14.000
so that whatever happens in the chastisement, they're all covered.

425
00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:17.000
That's terribly important.

426
00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:23.000
Jesus said, "I feel unfortunate with the poor one who feels the weight of his hunger.

427
00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:30.000
I feel the misfortune of many mothers whose hearts bleed for their sons in battle.

428
00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:39.000
I want to give you Isaiah 53.4."

429
00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:45.000
"Ah," he said, "all misfortunes weigh upon my heart, and I remain pierced.

430
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:50.000
And in the face of these misfortunes I see divine justice wanting to put out

431
00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:53.000
more divine fury into the field against humanity.

432
00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:58.000
Unfortunately, still rebellious and ungrateful."

433
00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:07.000
Now notice throughout these volumes, humanity is always identified as the ungrateful ones.

434
00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:12.000
And then who can tell how unfortunate I am in love?

435
00:32:12.000 --> 00:32:19.000
Souls do not love me, and my great love is repaid with repeated offenses.

436
00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:24.000
That's one of the things that Louisa does for us both in the Christmas novina

437
00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:33.000
and in the hours of the Passion is to put across to us the enormity of the love that Jesus has for us

438
00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:36.000
and the enormity of our ingratitude.

439
00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:41.000
I think they're put across very well in both of them.

440
00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:48.000
Now in the next paragraph he says that because of all the desperate spiritual need that's out there,

441
00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:54.000
that we should use whatever suffering that comes to us for souls.

442
00:32:54.000 --> 00:33:01.000
My daughter, he said, "In the midst of so many misfortunes of mine, instead of consoling you,

443
00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:03.000
I want to be comforted.

444
00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:08.000
I want souls who love me, who love to be around me."

445
00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:12.000
Now beside that I want to give you Mark 3.14.

446
00:33:12.000 --> 00:33:20.000
I want you to look souls around me, in Mark 3.14 you're told that Jesus called the Twelve Apostles

447
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:26.000
because he wanted them to be his companions, he wanted them to share with him.

448
00:33:26.000 --> 00:33:34.000
I want souls to love to be around me, that they may keep me faithful company.

449
00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:43.000
Okay, so we've got a step in there where others have stepped out and give all their pains to me.

450
00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:52.000
So the first thing you don't do is run for the Panadol.

451
00:33:52.000 --> 00:33:55.000
Maybe the last thing you don't do is run for the Panadol.

452
00:33:55.000 --> 00:34:01.000
Some of us have learned a little bit along the way and it's very liberating.

453
00:34:01.000 --> 00:34:07.000
Because the world today tells you no pain, no distress, no nothing.

454
00:34:07.000 --> 00:34:11.000
You must be going to wherever you're going to on cushions.

455
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:13.000
Life isn't like that.

456
00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:18.000
Whereas Jesus tells Louisa that everything that happens to us, absolutely everything,

457
00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:24.000
is divine currency to bring souls to him for eternity.

458
00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:29.000
And I'd rather have my headache and bring souls to him for eternity.

459
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:32.000
I'm only using that as an example, I don't have headaches.

460
00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:38.000
Okay, I think it's absolutely fantastic.

461
00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:43.000
I want souls to love to be around me, that they may keep me faithful company,

462
00:34:43.000 --> 00:34:51.000
that they give all their pains to me as a relief for my misfortunes and to impotrate.

463
00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:57.000
Now we usually say intercede, to intercede for grace, for the poor unfortunate ones,

464
00:34:57.000 --> 00:35:00.000
who are ever conditioned therein.

465
00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:05.000
Depending on whether souls are faithful to me in these times of scourges and misfortunes,

466
00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:11.000
once divine justice is appeased, I will reward the souls who have been faithful to me

